<Placemark><name>8:30 Leave Maruya Inn</name><description>Breakfast 7:30. Day 4 Course A: O-tsumago → Nagiso → Yogawa-michi → Nenoue Pass → Nojiri.

Path km 0.0 of 20.0.</description><styleUrl>#go</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>137.593000,35.564700,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9:00–9:45 Tsumago post town</name><description>Waki-honjin museum opens 9:00 (¥800; closed 2nd/4th Thursday). Guide: no more than an hour here. Leave by 9:45.

Path km 2.0 of 20.0.</description><styleUrl>#town</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>137.595000,35.579000,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>10:45–11:00 Nagiso Stn · buy picnic lunch</name><description>LAST EXIT: trains from here (Course B ends here). Buy the picnic lunch nearby. Leave 11:30–11:45.

Path km 5.9 of 20.0.</description><styleUrl>#exit</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>137.608400,35.598800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Optional · Momosuke Bridge</name><description>Wooden suspension bridge (1922) over the Kiso river, a short detour from Nagiso.

Path km 6.1 of 20.0.</description><styleUrl>#opt</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>137.606950,35.600880,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>12:15–12:30 Midono-juku → start Yogawa-michi climb</name><description>After Midono post town (三留野宿), climb the Yogawa-michi (与川道). From here there's no transport until Nojiri. Running late here? Think about Course B (train from Nagiso).

Path km 7.1 of 20.0.</description><styleUrl>#town</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>137.611560,35.608800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>≈13:35 Shozensawa stream (Yogawa / Midono boundary)</name><description>正善沢. On the way up the Yogawa valley.

Path km 10.2 of 20.0.</description><styleUrl>#pt</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>137.634550,35.621800,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>14:00–14:30 Picnic lunch ≈ Yogawa village headman's house</name><description>Guide: picnic lunch spot with a covered shelter at 14:00–14:30; this is the likely spot (与川村庄屋屋敷), not named in the guide. Leave 14:30–15:00.

Path km 12.0 of 20.0.</description><styleUrl>#lunch</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>137.641660,35.632060,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>15:45–16:00 Nenoue Pass (top)</name><description>根の上峠, the high point (~840 m). Sunset 16:40, dark ≈17:08: don't linger.

Path km 15.8 of 20.0.</description><styleUrl>#pass</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>137.655110,35.653180,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>17:00 Nojiri Stn · train 17:26 (or 14:52)</name><description>Donguri Café if you arrive before 16:45. Train 17:26 Nojiri → Kiso-Fukushima (38 min, ¥420), arrive 18:04; the earlier 14:52 if exceptionally fast. Then taxi (~¥900, 3–5 min) or walk ~1 km to Iwaya Inn. Dinner 19:00.

Path km 19.9 of 20.0.</description><styleUrl>#exit</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>137.636510,35.673170,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
